Step 3: Run the Application
Run your Next.js application:
npm run dev
Open your browser and navigate to http://localhost:3000. You should see the server-side rendered page.
Explanation
getServerSideProps: This function runs on the server for every request. It fetches data from an API and returns the data as props to the page component.
Home Component: This component receives the data as props and renders it. Since the data is fetched on the server, the HTML sent to the client will include the fully rendered content.
Hydration
Once the HTML is rendered and sent to the client, React will "hydrate" the static content. This means React will attach event listeners and make the page interactive without re-rendering the entire page. Hyd

