explain type casting in above example
1. Implicit Widening Cast (Automatic Promotion)
This happens inside the second while loop at this line:
sum += Math.pow(digit, digits);
The Setup: digit and digits are both declared as standard integers (int).
The Action: The Math.pow(double base, double exponent) method strictly expects two double arguments.
The Cast: Java automatically converts your int digit and int digits into double values before passing them to the function. This is a widening primitive conversion, which is completely safe and requires no extra syntax.
2. Compound Assignment Implicit Cast (The Hidden Narrowing)
The biggest type-casting magic happens when the result of Math.pow() comes back to be added to sum:
sum += Math.pow(digit, digits);
The Setup: Math.pow() always returns a double. Your variable sum is declared as an int.
