3. Key Differences: String vs. Data Structures
How to Make Strings "Dynamic"
Because String is immutable, appending text repeatedly creates multiple objects in memory. If you need a "dynamic string" structure that grows and modifies quickly without wasting memory, you should use StringBuilder or StringBuffer.
// Avoid doing this in heavy loops (creates a new object every time)
String str ="Hello";
str +=" World";// Do this instead for dynamic text manipulation
StringBuilder sb =new StringBuilder("Hello");
sb.append(" World");// Modifies the same object in memory
